## What changed in the inherited work

- paint-pot: the inherited build measured 0.095 m tall and showed spikes at the
  rim and the foot. The cause was profile.polygon(..., { smooth: true }): a closed
  Catmull-Rom spline overshoots at the two sharp corners of the wall section.
  The profile now uses a dense explicit point list, the pattern of assets/barrel.ts.
  The model measures 0.072 x 0.084 x 0.067 m and stands on y = 0.
- paint-pot: the inherited paint disc was wider than the cavity and poked through
  the wall. The paint is now a mound that fills the mouth of the cup.
- paint-pot: the cup is scaled by CUP_HEIGHT = 0.94. The render camera sits below
  the rim, so a pool inside the cup stays hidden in every delivery view. The
  ceramic body is 0.0798 m tall and the paint mound reaches 0.0845 m.
- paint-pot: the four colour presets stay red, blue, yellow, and green.
- brush: a new source. It is 0.17 m long, stands on its bristle tip, leans 8
  degrees toward +X, and is shifted along X so the mesh straddles the Y axis.
- brush: the grip band is real geometry (a cylinder of radius 0.0142 m from local
  y 0.126 to 0.154) on the handle body, not a painted band.
- brush: one body per material. The handle is wood, the ferrule is iron, and the
  bristles are cream with a red tip.
- ball, kite, and easel: unchanged from the inherited work.

